# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as
# CRLF while Biome formats them back to LF (its default lineEnding), so every
# `biome check --write` marks unrelated files as modified and `pnpm lint` fails
# on files nobody edited.
#
# .gitattributes wins over core.autocrlf and is checked in, so the rule holds
# for every clone rather than depending on each machine's git config. The repo
# already stores LF, so this pins existing behaviour rather than changing it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by the conversion above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
